  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  version: \"0.3.2\"\n\npackage:\n  name: multimark\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/posit-dev/multimark/archive/refs/tags/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 150bdd1ecd5af3c4b4bc12a099139862d9af6b51c48b3a229f5470a845075d00\n  patches:\n    - patches/use-system-cmark-gfm.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: 1\n  skip:\n    - linux and aarch64\n    - osx and arm64\n  script:\n    content: python -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n    env:\n      SETUPTOOLS_SCM_PRETEND_VERSION: ${{ version }}\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - if: build_platform != host_platform\n      then:\n        - python\n        - cross-python_${{ host_platform }}\n        - cffi\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n  host:\n    - python\n    - pip\n    - setuptools >=68\n    - setuptools_scm >=6.2\n    - cffi >=1.15\n    - cmark-gfm\n  run:\n    - python\n    - cffi >=1.15\n    - cmark-gfm\n    - click >=8.0\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - multimark\n      pip_check: true\n  - if: unix\n    then:\n      - script:\n          - multimark --help\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://github.com/posit-dev/multimark\n  repository: https://github.com/posit-dev/multimark\n  license: MIT AND BSD-2-Clause\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  summary: Python bindings to cmark-gfm — CommonMark parsing and rendering (HTML, LaTeX, man, XML, CommonMark)\n  description: |\n    multimark provides fast Python bindings to cmark-gfm, the C reference\n    implementation of CommonMark with GitHub Flavored Markdown extensions.\n\n    It exposes five output renderers — HTML, LaTeX, groff man, XML, and\n    normalized CommonMark — through a consistent, keyword-argument-based API.\n    All GFM extensions (tables, strikethrough, autolinks, task lists, tag\n    filtering) are supported, and raw HTML is safely stripped by default.\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - rich-iannone\n    - timkpaine\n",
